# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0100024> (self-limited familial infantile epilepsy)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8486-0558") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.epilepsydiagnosis.org/syndrome/benign-fam-nonfam-infantile-overview.html") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0100024> "This syndrome is characterized by the onset of seizures between 3 and 20 months of age (peak 6 months). Seizures may be frequent at onset but usually remit within 1 year from the onset. In untreated cases there can be isolated or brief clusters of seizures within the period from onset to remission. A minority of individuals may have epilepsy in later life. Some patients (with PRRT2 mutations) may develop paroxysmal kinesiogenic dyskinesia in later life.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000233> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0100024> "https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/5740"^^xsd:anyURI)
