# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0100225> (collagen 6-related myopathy)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21691338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40031/") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0100225> "A qualitative or quantitative defect of collagen 6 disorder that covers a wide spectrum of musculoskeletal phenotypes caused by dominant and recessive mutations in the three major collagen VI genes: COL6A1, COL6A2, and COL6A3. These variants lead to a variety of overlapping phenotypes, ranging from severe congenital muscle weakness, hypotonia, torticollis and contractures with loss or non-development of ambulation on one end and childhood to adult onset mild muscle weakness, stiffness, and joint hyperlaxity on the other.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000233> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0100225> "https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/2214"^^xsd:anyURI)
